It does matter by phase-of-game, though.  Your stance giving
reflection little value is for the late game.  Reflection grants
immunity to rays, and the ray wands are digging, magic missile,
cold, fire, lightning, sleep, death.  I don't think digging has an
effect on any player but the rest really matter to early game
players.

Because of this I tend to think that reflection is more important
in the early game, MR in the late game.  While I tend to spend
the early game preparing for th elate game, that strategy does
get my characters killed regularly.

Trying to tie this into comparing SDSM and GDSM in the early
game I suspect that the AC of any DSM is enough to make
magic missile, cold and fire survivable.  Also cold, fire, lightning
and sleep resistance can be acquired as intrinsics.  My play
strategy does include selectively eating monsters with the
resistance intrinsics in mind.  Yet another reason to make
SDSM less superior to GDSM in the early game.



